{
  "id": 92874852,
  "iid": 2482,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "IPPUSB: Do not assume every USB traffic is IPPUSB",
  "description": "It is invalid to assume that every unknown and/or vendor specific\ntraffic is IPPUSB. If a vendor specific class is indeed IPPUSB then\nthe dissector should be selected based on VID/PID.\n\nThe way IPPUSB was registering caused packets from devices without\ncorresponding dissector in Wireshark (majority of the devices in the\nwild) being dissected as IPPUSB and shown as Malformed Packets. For\nexample the Silicon Labs CP210x UART Bridge was dissected as IPPUSB.",
  "state": "merged",
